While the approach of the HKMA, as Hong Kong 's resolution authority, should be to coordinate cross -
border resolution action(s) with the resolution authorities concerned, the HKMA may take actions which 
do not align with those of such resolution authorities. The HKMA may make one or more bail -in 
instruments (which may include both senior and subordinated in scope unsecured liabilities) in respect of a 
within scope financial institution (as defined in the FIRO). Such power may also be applied to the holding 
company of a within scope financial institution (each as defined in the FIRO) in the same way, and to the 
same extent, as if the holding company (including, in this case, the Issuer) were a within scope financial 
